{
  "name": "std-site-header",
  "description": "std-site-header — the sticky top bar of a public website: brand (logo + name), navigation links with the current page marked, and an optional call-to-action button. On small screens the links fold into a menu opened by a toggle. Links follow `href` (in-app path, #anchor, or absolute URL); the header action and the small-screen menu links also emit NAV_CLICKED { href, label }. Pick for marketing sites, docs portals and product websites; for signed-in app chrome use std-app-layout.",
  "level": "atom",
  "topic": "ui/core",
  "schema": {
